//Data Members or Member Variables

Data members are the variables declared inside a class.

Example:

class Student {
public:
    string name;
    int age;
};

Here:

name → data member
age → data member

Each object gets its own copy of these data members.

Student s1;
Student s2;

s1.age = 20;
s2.age = 25;

Here s1.age and s2.age are separate.

Simple definition:

Data members are variables inside a class that store the data/state of an object.